{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Why do you quarrel with me.</b> Do you not know that I am commanded and act accordingly?" "<b>Why do you test HaShem.</b> And if your quarrel is with me in order to test the One who sent me — why do you test to your own harm? For this testing carries great danger: if He grows wrathful, He may show His action to destroy you, and the testing turn out evil for you. As it says: בְּחָנוּנִי גַּם רָאוּ פָעֳלִי (Psalms 95:9) — that is, to their own harm."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:55.761958144Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}